## Issue-driven development + dev diary

Work happens in an **issue** (feature/fix/ci/docs). The issue is the “source of truth”.

Required:
- issue contains **AC + test plan + docs impact** (see `02-work-item-definition.mdc`)
- development progress is tracked in **issue comments** (dev diary)

### Dev diary comment template

```markdown
## Dev diary – YYYY-MM-DD
What changed:
- ...

Why:
- ...

Evidence:
- Tests: <local/CI output>
- Manual: <steps + result>

Docs:
- Updated: <files — include docs/dokumentace/domeny/… when src/irswitch changed>
- Pending: <files>
- Or: Docs: no change (reason …)

Next:
- ...

Risks:
- ...
```

### Minimal cadence

- Add a diary entry when you:
  - push a meaningful chunk of work
  - discover a blocker/root cause
  - change the plan/AC

